map.story:
write_map(path, m) saves the map object m as a JSON file at path.
It writes four fields in order: file, links, terms, and map.
Example: with links [{"name": "emit"}], the file holds "links": [
    {"name": "emit"}
  ].
Each link and each term takes one line. Empty lists become []. The tree nodes come from write_node.
